fn text_intern(text: Text) -> Text effects []

// Ensure a text value has process-lifetime storage.
// Use this when a scoped arena-allocated text must outlive its arena scope,
// such as when storing into a global data structure or returning from
// an [alloc]-free function. Interned texts are never freed and each
// unique content is stored exactly once (deduplicated via FNV-1a hash).
//
// Use cases:
//   - Promoting temporary arena text to persistent storage
//   - Avoiding use-after-free diagnostics when text crosses scope boundaries
//   - Reducing memory footprint through deduplication of repeated values
//
// Example:
//   fn make_persistent_label(prefix: Text, suffix: Text) -> Text {
//       text_intern(text_concat(prefix, suffix))
//   }
